<article class="env-lemma" id="0FNQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FNQ">Lemma <span data-tag="0FNQ">15.128.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. The derived category $D(R)$ of $R$ is a symmetric monoidal category with tensor product given by derived tensor product and associativity and commutativity constraints as in Section <a href="/tag/0FNG" data-tag="0FNG">15.74</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hints: The associativity constraint is the isomorphism of Lemma <a href="/tag/0BYJ" data-tag="0BYJ">15.60.15</a> and the commutativity constraint is the isomorphism of Lemma <a href="/tag/0BYI" data-tag="0BYI">15.60.14</a>. Having said this the commutativity of various diagrams follows from the corresponding result for the category of complexes of $R$-modules, see Section <a href="/tag/0GWN" data-tag="0GWN">15.59</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>